Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. GUESTHOUSE - MONDAY MORNING

Ruth appears on the laptop. Zoe's notebook faces her; Elias sits beyond the camera.

ZOE
Detonation.

RUTH
Controlled disclosure in anything I write.

Zoe has three rules: no whole-drive dump, no unrelated children used to prove adult conduct, no sole copy of the truth.

Ruth qualifies them honestly. Jackie own information may be necessary to investigate Jackie. Police may lawfully require relevant records. Zoe cannot decide every other child's interests.

Zoe acknowledges each limit. Her original drive and personal folder remain closed.

Ruth identifies separate recipients and scope: institutions for their authority records; investigators for contractor/current-coercion and verification evidence; counsel for adult sponsor and payment material.

Journalist Daniel Rusk receives less: redacted contradiction, chronology, authenticated adult sponsor link and questions he can check independently. No girls' names, no statements or child files.

DANIEL (SPEAKER)
This is thin.

ZOE
It's supposed to be. Check it.

INT. DANIEL'S WORKSPACE - MORNING

Daniel calls published institutional contacts. North Vale confirms the real base reference, unsupported supplemental powers. Westmere confirms a restricted subset under review, not all placements. Priya confirms signed contractor accounts, not knowing use of forged orders. Mac's counsel authenticates AC019 and the signature, not every referral as criminal.

His draft includes WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED. No total victim count. No claim all Westmere work was unlawful.

INT. GUESTHOUSE - 10:00

RUTH
Ready?

ZOE
No whole archive. No Jackie to the press.

RUTH
Agreed.

ZOE
Do it.

Acknowledgements arrive from different recipients. Nothing explodes. Zoe switches off the receiver.

INT. INTERVIEW SUITES / LEGAL COMPANY - DAY

Voss and Vale give separate accounts consistent in their essential facts. Neither receives a deal for good faith.

Verification templates and relevant logs are preserved through forensic handling. The legal administrator who refused Cain signs a handover.

Mac's voluntary police interview changes status. He is cautioned; counsel checks whether he still intends to cooperate. He does.

EXT. A49 LAY-BY - AFTERNOON

Cain's new solicitor asks authority to share his location. Cain agrees. Later officers arrest him on suspicion of offences connected with Jackie and related matters. Hands visible. No fight, no verdict.

INT. GUESTHOUSE - LATE AFTERNOON

The independently checked article remains narrow. Zoe asks what happens if a reviewed case proves normal.

RUTH
It should be recorded as normal.

Publication risks remain; the investigations would continue if they waited. Zoe accepts the limited draft after those answers. Other outlets begin their own questions.

Ruth reads one sentence from Helen only after Zoe agrees: later care did not make the original choice theirs to make.

ZOE
Stop there.

Ruth stops.

INT. GUESTHOUSE - EVENING

Zoe crosses out DETONATION. Writes IRREVERSIBLE.

She takes out the drive and her numbered folder. They are not the same thing. Negotiates with Ruth: protected evidential handover for the original, separate solicitor custody for her folder, each with its own receipt and lawful limits.

She seals the folder in an envelope. Writes ZOE across the flap.

ZOE
I don't want to carry that drive anymore.

ELIAS
You don't have to carry it to keep it true.

Tomorrow's bag is zipped closed.
